{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CubicSaddleDiscriminant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.CubicSaddleDiscriminant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CubicSaddleDiscriminant.five_two_saddle_diff_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CubicSaddleDiscriminant.five_two_saddle_diff_sq","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CubicSaddleDiscriminant.lean#L44-L57","doc":"**The three 5₂ saddle differences square to `−23`.** For three saddles of the\n`u = 0` cubic `y³ − 2y² + 3y − 1` (Vieta: `Σy = 2`, `Σyᵢyⱼ = 3`, `∏y = 1`), the\nproduct of their squared pairwise differences is the trace-field discriminant\n`−23` — the geometric (root-difference) form of\n`FiveTwoSaddleCurve.u0_cubic_discriminant`, exhibiting `−23` as\n`∏_{i<j}(V_i − V_j)`-square of the exact saddle singularities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CubicSaddleDiscriminant.disc_eq_root_diff_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CubicSaddleDiscriminant.disc_eq_root_diff_sq","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CubicSaddleDiscriminant.lean#L30-L42","doc":"**Cubic discriminant as the product of squared root differences.** For any\nthree ring elements (the three saddles), the square of the product of their\npairwise differences equals the discriminant written in the elementary symmetric\nfunctions `e₁ = Σyᵢ`, `e₂ = Σyᵢyⱼ`, `e₃ = ∏yᵢ`:\n`((y₁−y₂)(y₂−y₃)(y₃−y₁))² = e₁²e₂² − 4e₂³ − 4e₁³e₃ + 18e₁e₂e₃ − 27e₃²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}